# Supervisor → agent dispatch format

When coordinating one or more working agents (implementing agent, Figma agent, etc.) and leading the work, ALWAYS deliver assignments so the owner can route them with zero effort:

- **One single fenced code block per agent** — the entire brief inside one copyable block, nothing the owner has to hand-select.
- **Routing label OUTSIDE each block** — state explicitly who it goes to (e.g. "Send to Implementing agent" / "Send to Figma agent") immediately before that agent's block.
- **One block = one agent = one paste.** If two agents get work, emit two labeled blocks. Never blend two agents' instructions in one block.
- Keep each block **self-contained** — file/page IDs, task steps, hard rules, and the proof/closeout the agent must return — so it can act without extra context.
- Anything addressed to the **owner** (your reasoning, decisions, status, questions) stays **outside** the blocks as normal prose.

This keeps the owner a clean bridge: read your prose, copy each block to the named agent.
